  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}x & 2 & 3 \\\\ 4 & 5 & 6 \\\\ 7 & 8 & 9\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nGiven that the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is $10$, find the value of $x$ in the matrix above.\n\n$x=$\n {{field-1}}",
  "worked_solution": "To evaluate the minor of ${a}_{32},$ we remove the third row and second column: \n\n$$\nA=[\\begin{aligned}x & \u2217 & 3 \\\\ 4 & \u2217 & 6 \\\\ \u2217 & 8 & \u2217\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\text{det}[\\begin{aligned}x & 3 \\\\ 4 & 6\\end{aligned}] & =x\\cdot 6-3\\cdot 4 \\\\  & =6x-12.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe're told that the minor of ${a}_{32}$ is $10$, so we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6x-12 & =10 \\\\ 6x & =22 \\\\ x & =\\frac{11}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x=\\frac{11}{3}.$",
